<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen firmer, rate cut could lift.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen firmer, rate cut could lift.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 9.00 a.m./2300 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2676.40   -7.00   DJIA  cl	8116.93  +28.57</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2705     +10   US 30yr cl	 6.44   +0.01</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.560  -0.020   Gold NY 324.25 Lon fix 321.95</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7350 (Thu 0.7363)   CRB Index cl   237.74   +1.46</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20286.23 +155.72   FTSE cl	 4862.90  -11.60</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   946.10   +0.25   NZSE40	  2498.03   +5.73</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 25)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen firmer early, eye on RBA, rate cut go-ahead likely to boost market. &quot;If they cut rates our market will accept that extremely well and move up,&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$17.88 (steady), A$19.02 (-.03), A$6.17 (-.03), A$7.59 (steady)</p>
<p>*Wall Street stocks posted moderate gains with the market bouncing back from a brief foray below the 8,000 level.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-3/16 (+1/16), BHP 26-1/4 (-9/16), WMC 22-11/16 (-4/16), National Australia Bank 70-1/2 (-1-3/4)</p>
<p>*Gold price was higher. On LME zinc and aluminium powered higher as spreads tightened. Copper firmed, nickel steady.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
